      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T16:49:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this would require that we dynamically define sk_FragColor rather than statically defining it with an index in sksl_frag.sksl. My understanding is that though it always has a kind of \"logical\" index of 0, we can only emit that in WGSL if we\u0027ve enabled dual-source blending (per https://crsrc.org/c/third_party/dawn/docs/dawn/features/dual_source_blending.md and verified by testing).\n\nWe\u0027d want to have a check for `index \u003e\u003d 0` anyways, since uniforms declarations are written here and have an index of -1, which we wouldn\u0027t want to emit.\n\nMaybe this could all be expressed better, or at least have a comment separate from the assert\u0027s comment? And maybe the assert is superfluous since invalid code emitted here will be caught by the WGSL compiler anyways.",
      "parentUuid": "b4136976_89cfd2e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1247,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1251,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "47dd14e711b18000306b3e4298e5bbbaac925108",
